      "body": "## Overview\n\nLog DP coordinator out-of-order step reports at DEBUG instead of WARNING. Reports from different engines can arrive in a different step order even when each engine reports in order.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Avoid per-report warning output for cross-engine statistics arrival skew at the default log level; retain the diagnostic at DEBUG.\n- Preserve all statistics updates, step snapshots, and wave coordination.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Existing run evidence: a saved audit of a 32-rank DP deployment counted 1,751,591 occurrences, totaling 290,881,789 bytes. All reports had the same wave as the global latest report; 1,751,578 lagged by one step and 13 by two steps. This is evidence of logging volume, not a measured throughput improvement.\n- `ruff check vllm/v1/engine/coordinator.py` — passed.\n- `ruff format --check vllm/v1/engine/coordinator.py` — passed.\n- `python -m py_compile vllm/v1/engine/coordinator.py` — passed, using the existing venv.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- `pre-commit run --files vllm/v1/engine/coordinator.py docs/usage/troubleshooting.md` — all applicable checks passed, including mypy and Markdown lint.\n- Tests and model evaluations were not run. The sole executable change is the diagnostic level; no inference or statistics-processing behavior changes. No new test was added solely to assert log severity. Runtime validation remains pending for this draft.\n\n## Details\n\nThe comparison is against one global `(wave, step)` position. For example, engine A's step 101 may arrive before engine B's step 100, causing a warning even if B's previous report was step 99. The warning alone does not establish same-engine message regression or a failed request.\n\nThis is a logging-only alternative to #52936, which adds per-engine position tracking and rejects regressing reports. It does not add state or discard reports, and it does not claim to repair cross-engine snapshot consistency. The original snapshot/load-balancing design from #21617 remains intact. Open-PR searches found #52936 but no separate logging-only fix.\n\nThe troubleshooting guide documents the diagnostic and how to enable it with `VLLM_LOGGING_LEVEL=DEBUG`. The tradeoff is reduced default visibility of this ordering diagnostic, including any anomalous cases that reach the same branch.\n\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex prepared the patch and PR (the exact underlying model version was not exposed); `moonshotai/Kimi-K3` assisted with source analysis and checklist review. This is a draft for human review.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
